---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<Layout title="Protect PLG | Prospect Lefferts Gardens">

<!-- ─── HERO ─── -->
<section class="hero">
  <Nav activePage="home" />

  <div class="hero-body">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span>Prospect Lefferts Gardens, Brooklyn</span></p>
    <h1 class="hero-headline">
      Protect <em>PLG.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      A resident-led campaign for contextual zoning, transparent development, and affordable-housing commitments that are specific and in writing.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a href="#join" class="btn-primary">Join the Neighborhood-Wide Effort</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── CENTRAL MESSAGE ─── -->
<section class="creed-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="creed reveal">
      <p>Much of Prospect Lefferts Gardens remains governed by an R6 zoning framework created in the 1960s. Unlike many surrounding neighborhoods, PLG does not have consistent contextual rules governing the height, bulk, and setbacks of new buildings. <em>Protect PLG</em> is organizing for a neighborhood-wide planning process that establishes reasonable, predictable standards and demands clear affordability commitments before the next major project is already underway.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── OUR LONG-TERM GOALS ─── -->
<section class="about" id="goals">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <p class="section-label">Our Long-Term Goals</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Contextual zoning and <em>affordability in writing.</em></h2>
      <p>We are asking the Department of City Planning to begin a comprehensive contextual-zoning study for Prospect Lefferts Gardens, with meaningful participation from residents, elected officials, and the community board. We are also asking developers and property owners to put any affordable-housing promises in clear, specific terms.</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="facts-list reveal" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">A comprehensive contextual-zoning study</span> led by the Department of City Planning.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Neighborhood-supported height, bulk, and setback rules</span> appropriate to PLG's residential streets.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Affordable-housing commitments that specify</span> the number of units, income levels served, duration of affordability, and enforcement mechanism in writing.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Clear public information about major development proposals</span>, including approved plans and the zoning basis for each project.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Consistent review and enforcement</span> of zoning, permitting, FAR, open-space, and air-rights requirements.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Clearly defined community benefits</span> when a developer or property owner uses those benefits to justify a project.</div></li>
    </ul>

    <p class="list-note reveal">Contextual zoning does not automatically create affordable housing. Protect PLG treats these as related but separate goals: establishing predictable rules for future development and demanding clear, documented affordability commitments when projects proceed.</p>

    <div class="housing-position reveal">
      <p class="section-label" style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">Where We Stand on Development</p>
      <p>We are not calling for a ban on all construction. We believe PLG has already absorbed substantial market-rate development and should have contextual rules that set reasonable limits on height and bulk. When new housing is proposed, any promise of affordability should be specific and in writing, including the number of units, income levels served, duration of affordability, and how the commitment will be enforced.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── WHY DOES THIS KEEP HAPPENING ─── -->
<section class="about" id="why" style="background:var(--black); border-top:1px solid rgba(200,40,26,0.2); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(200,40,26,0.2);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <p class="section-label">The Bigger Picture</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Why does this <em>keep happening?</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="about-body reveal">
      <p>Most of Prospect Lefferts Gardens is zoned R6, a 1960s "Tower in the Park" framework with a floor-area ratio of 2.43 and <strong>no height limit</strong>. Nearby neighborhoods such as Park Slope, Windsor Terrace, and Kensington received contextual zoning with height limits years ago. <strong>PLG did not.</strong> That gap is why a 12-story building pencils out here and a five-story building pencils out one neighborhood over.</p>
      <p>PLG's zoning was last comprehensively updated in <strong>1961</strong>, and the community has been formally asking the Department of City Planning for a <strong>contextual rezoning study since 2008</strong>. On PLG's large lots, the current rules reward demolishing smaller buildings and replacing them with much bigger ones.</p>
      <p>Prospect Lefferts Gardens has added thousands of housing units over the past decade, much of it market-rate, while rents have continued to rise beyond what many residents can afford. Protect PLG believes the neighborhood's next chapter should be guided by a comprehensive planning process rather than a series of unrelated as-of-right projects evaluated only after plans have been filed.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="sec-head reveal" style="margin-top:3.5rem;">
      <p class="section-label">How the Process Works</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="facts-list reveal">
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">As-of-right building.</span> If a project fits the existing zoning, the developer can build it with DOB permits alone, with no public hearing and no City Council vote.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">DOB review.</span> The Department of Buildings checks plans against the zoning and building code, including FAR, open space, and any air-rights transfers. Its records are public, but not always easy to read.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">ULURP.</span> The Uniform Land Use Review Procedure is the public process that runs through the community board, borough president, City Planning Commission, and City Council. It is only triggered when a project needs a zoning change, variance, or special permit. An as-of-right building skips it entirely.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Contextual rezoning.</span> A neighborhood-wide zoning change, run through ULURP, is the tool that would bring height and setback rules in line with the existing streets across PLG.</div></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── THE 331 MAPLE STREET CASE ─── -->
<section class="about" id="case">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="before-after reveal">
      <div class="ba-card">
        <div class="ba-label ba-label-before">Demolished, 2026</div>
        <img src="/331mapleparish.png" alt="The former parish school at 335 Maple St, built 1909" />
        <p class="ba-caption">The 335 Maple St parish school, built 1909. Demolished in 2026.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ba-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="ba-card">
        <div class="ba-label ba-label-after">Under construction</div>
        <img src="/331maplemockup.png" alt="Developer rendering of the building at 331 Maple St" />
        <p class="ba-caption">Developer rendering of the 12-story, 118-foot, 99-unit building now under construction. Affordability terms have not been made public.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sec-head reveal" style="margin-top:4rem;">
      <p class="section-label">Case Study: 331 Maple Street</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">How one project <em>unfolded.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="about-body reveal">
      <p>Protect PLG began in response to the redevelopment of 331&ndash;335 Maple Street. The parish school has now been demolished and the replacement building is under construction. This campaign does not present the project as something it still expects to stop. Instead, the case documents how the current zoning and as-of-right development process can leave residents trying to understand major decisions only after they are already well underway.</p>
      <p>The land is owned by the Roman Catholic parish of St. Francis of Assisi and St. Blaise, which signed a long-term ground lease with developer <strong>Candor Capital</strong>. In August 2025, plans were filed with the Department of Buildings for a 12-story, 118-foot building with 99 apartments and about 24,000 square feet of community-facility space, on an R6 lot <span class="cite">(<a href="https://commercialobserver.com/2025/08/candor-capital-housing-331-maple-street-brooklyn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Commercial Observer</a>, <a href="https://brooklyneagle.com/articles/2025/08/22/brooklyn-developer-files-plans-for-99-apartments-on-church-owned-lot" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brooklyn Eagle</a>, <a href="https://newyorkyimby.com/2025/09/permits-filed-for-331-maple-street-in-prospect-lefferts-gardens-brooklyn.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NY YIMBY</a>)</span>.</p>
      <p>According to Father Thomas Vassalotti, church leadership was shown a six-story concept before the lease was signed; the plans filed with DOB were for twelve stories. Because the project is largely as-of-right, there was no public hearing.</p>
      <p>In January 2026, demolition activity began at 335 Maple Street before the required permits were issued. DOB issued a <strong>Stop Work Order</strong>, and the developer went on to receive violations and fines totaling roughly <strong>$30,000</strong>. The 1909 parish school was demolished later that year, and construction is now underway.</p>
      <p>Questions about the project's zoning basis remain open. Community members who have reviewed ACRIS records have not identified a recorded air-rights transfer between the development lot and the larger church lot that would support the building's floor area. Residents have asked DOB and City Planning to confirm the FAR calculation and publish the review. Affordability terms for the building have not been made public.</p>

      <p class="section-label" style="margin-top:2.75rem;">What 331 Maple Shows</p>
      <p>331 Maple Street demonstrates why reacting project by project is not enough. By the time most residents understand the zoning, permits, property records, and development plans involved, the most consequential decisions may already have been made. Protect PLG is using this case to advocate for neighborhood-wide contextual zoning, clearer public information, and written affordability commitments before the next major proposal is underway.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── NEIGHBOR VOICES ─── -->
<section class="quotes-strip">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <p class="section-label" style="color:rgba(245,239,224,0.4);">Neighbor Voices</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">What residents said when the <em>plans became public.</em></h2>
      <p>These comments were collected as the 331 Maple Street proposal first became public and before the parish school was demolished. They reflect individual residents' concerns at that moment and document why the community began organizing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="quotes-cta reveal">
      <a href="/voices" class="btn-outline">Read the Original Neighbor Voices</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── JOIN THE EFFORT ─── -->
<section class="join-section" id="join">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <p class="section-label">Join the PLG-Wide Effort</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Help plan <em>what comes next.</em></h2>
      <p class="join-intro">Protect PLG is building resident support for contextual zoning and greater accountability around future development. Neighbors can help by attending meetings, researching public records, tracking development filings, canvassing, and reaching others across the neighborhood.</p>
    </div>

    <form id="join-form" class="join-form reveal" action="https://api.web3forms.com/submit" method="POST">
      <input type="hidden" name="access_key" value="207bb50e-9621-42c1-bafe-c8887e520c31" />
      <input type="hidden" name="subject" value="New Protect PLG signup" />
      <input type="hidden" name="from_name" value="Protect PLG website" />
      <input type="checkbox" name="botcheck" class="join-hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />

      <div class="join-field">
        <label for="join-name">Name</label>
        <input type="text" id="join-name" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
      </div>

      <div class="join-field">
        <label for="join-email">Email</label>
        <input type="email" id="join-email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
      </div>

      <fieldset class="join-field join-check-group">
        <legend class="join-legend">How I can help</legend>
        <label class="join-check"><input type="checkbox" name="help" value="Canvassing" /> Canvassing</label>
        <label class="join-check"><input type="checkbox" name="help" value="Attending meetings" /> Attending meetings</label>
        <label class="join-check"><input type="checkbox" name="help" value="Research" /> Research</label>
        <label class="join-check"><input type="checkbox" name="help" value="Outreach" /> Outreach</label>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="join-field">
        <label for="join-message">Message <span style="text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0;">(optional)</span></label>
        <textarea id="join-message" name="message"></textarea>
      </div>

      <button type="submit" class="btn-primary join-submit">Join Protect PLG</button>
      <p class="join-error" id="join-error" hidden>Something went wrong sending that. Please try again in a moment.</p>
    </form>

    <div class="join-success" id="join-success" hidden>
      <p><strong>Thank you. You're on the list.</strong> We'll reach out with next steps and meeting information.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<Footer />

<script>
  // Join form — submit to Web3Forms via fetch, show inline success state
  const form = document.getElementById('join-form') as HTMLFormElement | null;
  if (form) {
    const errBox = document.getElementById('join-error');
    const successBox = document.getElementById('join-success');
    const submitBtn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]') as HTMLButtonElement | null;
    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (errBox) errBox.hidden = true;
      if (submitBtn) { submitBtn.disabled = true; submitBtn.textContent = 'Sending…'; }
      try {
        const res = await fetch(form.action, {
          method: 'POST',
          body: new FormData(form),
          headers: { Accept: 'application/json' },
        });
        const data = await res.json();
        if (res.ok && data.success) {
          form.hidden = true;
          if (successBox) successBox.hidden = false;
          successBox?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
        } else {
          throw new Error(data.message || 'Request failed');
        }
      } catch {
        if (submitBtn) { submitBtn.disabled = false; submitBtn.textContent = 'Join Protect PLG'; }
        if (errBox) errBox.hidden = false;
      }
    });
  }

  // Scroll reveal
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const els = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
    if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window)) { els.forEach(el => el.classList.add('visible')); return; }
    const obs = new IntersectionObserver((entries, o) => {
      entries.forEach(e => { if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('visible'); o.unobserve(e.target); } });
    }, { threshold: 0.08 });
    els.forEach(el => obs.observe(el));
  });
</script>

</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .hero {
    background: var(--black);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero::before { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; background: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 60% at 50% 120%, #C8281A22 0%, transparent 70%); pointer-events: none; }
  .hero::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 256 256' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='noise'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.9' numOctaves='4' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23noise)' opacity='0.06'/%3E%3C/svg%3E"); pointer-events: none; opacity: 0.4; }
  .hero-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; text-align: center; padding: 5.5rem 2rem 5rem; position: relative; z-index: 5; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--red); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; max-width: 100%; animation: fadeUp 0.8s ease both; }
  .eyebrow span { display: inline-block; background: rgba(200,40,26,0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(200,40,26,0.4); padding: 0.3rem 0.9rem; border-radius: 2px; max-width: 100%; }
  .hero-headline { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(3rem, 10vw, 9rem); line-height: 0.92; letter-spacing: 0.02em; max-width: 100%; animation: fadeUp 0.8s 0.15s ease both; }
  .hero-headline em { font-style: normal; color: var(--red); }
  .hero-sub { width: min(640px, 100%); margin: 2rem auto 0; font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.65; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.7); animation: fadeUp 0.8s 0.3s ease both; }
  .hero-sub strong { color: var(--cream); font-weight: 500; }
  .hero-ctas { display: flex; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; animation: fadeUp 0.8s 0.45s ease both; align-items: center; }

  /* ─── QUOTES STRIP ─── */
  .quotes-strip { background: rgba(245,239,224,0.03); border-top: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.07); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.07); padding: 5rem 2rem; }
  .quotes-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .quotes-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 2rem; }
  .pull-quote { margin: 0; padding: 2rem; background: rgba(245,239,224,0.04); border: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.08); border-top: 3px solid var(--red); display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .pull-quote p { font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.8); margin: 0; }
  .pull-quote footer { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.2rem; }
  .pull-quote footer strong { font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--cream); font-style: normal; }
  .pull-quote footer span { font-size: 0.73rem; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.4); letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .quotes-cta { text-align: center; margin-top: 3rem; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .quotes-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; } }

  .about { background: var(--warm-gray); padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; }
  .about-body { max-width: 800px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .sec-head { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto 2.75rem; text-align: center; }
  .sec-head p:not([class]) { color: rgba(245,239,224,0.6); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .sec-head .section-title { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .about-body p { color: rgba(245,239,224,0.72); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; font-size: 1.02rem; }
  .about-body strong { color: var(--cream); font-weight: 500; }
  .about-body a { color: rgba(200,40,26,0.95); text-decoration: none; }
  .about-body a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .cite { font-size: 0.9rem; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.5); }
  .facts-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; max-width: 800px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .facts-list li { padding: 1.1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.1); display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 0.95rem; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.7); line-height: 1.55; }
  .facts-list li:first-child { border-top: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.1); }
  .fact-icon { color: var(--red); font-size: 0.7rem; margin-top: 0.38rem; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .fact-strong { color: var(--cream); font-weight: 500; }

  .list-note { max-width: 800px; margin: 1.75rem auto 0; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.55); }

  .housing-position { background: rgba(245,239,224,0.04); border: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.12); border-left: 4px solid var(--red); padding: 1.8rem 2rem; margin: 3rem auto 0; max-width: 800px; }
  .housing-position p:last-child { color: rgba(245,239,224,0.8); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 1.02rem; }

  .before-after { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: center; }
  .ba-card { position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .ba-card img { width: 100%; height: 320px; object-fit: cover; display: block; filter: brightness(0.9); }
  .ba-label { position: absolute; top: 1rem; left: 1rem; font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem; z-index: 2; font-weight: 500; }
  .ba-label-before { background: rgba(14,14,14,0.85); color: var(--cream); border: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.3); }
  .ba-label-after { background: rgba(200,40,26,0.9); color: #fff; }
  .ba-caption { font-size: 0.75rem; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.45); padding: 0.7rem 0 0; line-height: 1.4; font-style: italic; }
  .ba-arrow { font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--red); opacity: 0.6; font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; text-align: center; }

  .creed-section { background: var(--cream); color: var(--black); padding: 6rem 2rem; }
  .creed { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; }
  .creed p { font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2.1rem); line-height: 1.45; color: var(--black); }
  .creed em { font-style: italic; color: var(--dark-red); }

  /* ─── JOIN FORM ─── */
  .join-section { background: var(--black); border-top: 1px solid rgba(200,40,26,0.2); }
  .join-intro { color: rgba(245,239,224,0.55); max-width: 620px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0.5rem auto 0; }
  .join-form { max-width: 620px; margin: 2.75rem auto 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.4rem; }
  .join-field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.45rem; border: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .join-field label, .join-legend { font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.5); padding: 0; }
  .join-field input[type="text"], .join-field input[type="email"], .join-field textarea {
    background: rgba(245,239,224,0.04); border: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.18); color: var(--cream);
    padding: 0.8rem 0.95rem; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 0.98rem; border-radius: 2px; width: 100%;
  }
  .join-field input:focus, .join-field textarea:focus { outline: none; border-color: var(--red); background: rgba(245,239,224,0.06); }
  .join-field textarea { min-height: 110px; resize: vertical; }
  .join-check-group { gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .join-check { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.98rem; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.8); letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none; cursor: pointer; }
  .join-check input { width: 1.05rem; height: 1.05rem; accent-color: var(--red); flex-shrink: 0; }
  .join-hp { position: absolute !important; left: -9999px !important; opacity: 0 !important; height: 0; width: 0; }
  .join-submit { align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  .join-submit:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: default; transform: none; }
  .join-error { background: rgba(200,40,26,0.12); border: 1px solid rgba(200,40,26,0.45); color: #f2c9c3; padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .join-success { background: rgba(34,197,94,0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(34,197,94,0.4); border-left: 4px solid #22c55e; color: #d7f5e0; padding: 1.6rem 1.8rem; margin: 2.5rem auto 0; max-width: 620px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .join-success strong { color: #fff; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .before-after { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .ba-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); text-align: center; }
    .ba-card img { height: 240px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .hero-body { padding: 3rem 1.2rem 2.5rem; }
    .hero-ctas { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
    .about { padding-top: 2.5rem; padding-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .creed-section { padding: 4rem 1.2rem; }
    .sec-head { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 400px) {
    .hero-sub { font-size: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
